========================================================================================================================
PART 2.  PROVENANCE.  Where does each of g05's four hard-coded dispersions actually come from?
========================================================================================================================
  Baumgardt's parameter table column 22 is sigma0[km/s] -- the CENTRAL velocity dispersion of his fitted
  N-body MODEL.  His separate profile table carries the MEASURED dispersion in radial bins, with star counts.
  The Wolf et al. 2010 estimator that g05 inverts wants the dispersion AT r_1/2, not the model centre.

  cluster     g05 used  sigma0 (MODEL)                   measured bins (R arcsec: sigma, N)   at r_hl
  Pal 4           0.87            0.80                                     27": 0.88 (N=23)     0.880
  Pal 14          0.38            0.70                                     77": 0.71 (N=16)     0.710
  Pal 3           0.80            0.80                                     24": 1.70 (N=22)     1.700
  NGC 2419        5.10            5.10 38": 5.51 (N=62); 100": 2.63 (N=62); 214": 1.64 (N=59)     4.771
  
  PUBLISHED DIRECT MEASUREMENTS, carried alongside: Pal 14 sigma = 0.38 +- 0.12 km/s from 16 members
     (Jordi et al. 2009, AJ 137, 4586); Pal 4 sigma = 0.87 +- 0.18 km/s from 23 members (Frank et al. 2012,
     MNRAS 423, 2917).  Baumgardt's own bins on the SAME stars give 0.71 and 0.88.
  [PASS] V2 (THE PROVENANCE IS NOT WHAT THE CLAIM SAYS IT IS) g05 describes Pal 3 and NGC 2419 as coming 'from Baumgardt's own N-body fits'.  They come from ONE COLUMN of that fit -- sigma0, the MODEL CENTRAL dispersion -- and g05 then feeds that central value into a Wolf et al. 2010 estimator that is defined at the half-light radius.  Baumgardt's separately tabulated MEASURED dispersions for those same two clusters exist, are in this repository, and are used by this repository's own committed h93_outer_halo_globulars.py   (exact column matches to sigma0: Pal 4=not sigma0, Pal 14=not sigma0, Pal 3=sigma0, NGC 2419=sigma0)
  [FAIL] V3 (THE SMOKING GUN, AND IT FAILS) for Pal 3 the model central dispersion g05 uses and the measured dispersion Baumgardt tabulates from the SAME 22 stars the model was fitted to disagree by a factor of more than two.  Pal 3 is the ONE cluster of the four whose measurement the N-body model does not reproduce -- for Pal 4 and Pal 14 the model sigma0 and the measured bin agree to 10 per cent -- and it is precisely that cluster where g05 substitutes the model number for the measurement.  The substitution moves Pal 3 by 0.65 dex in the direction that supports the claim.  This repository's own h93 uses the measured 1.70 and states in its check 93f that 'Pal 3 goes the OTHER way ... a problem for Newton and a point FOR the framework'   (Pal 3: g05 uses sigma = 0.80 km/s (Baumgardt sigma0, model central); Baumgardt's MEASURED bin is 1.70 +0.38/-0.30 km/s from 22 stars at 11.1 pc.  Ratio 2.12, i.e. +0.655 dex in acceleration.  For comparison the model reproduces the measurement for Pal 4 (0.80 vs 0.88) and Pal 14 (0.70 vs 0.71))
  [FAIL] V4 (an APERTURE error, this repository's own listed bug pattern, and it fails) NGC 2419's dispersion profile falls by a factor 3.4 from 16 pc to 92 pc.  g05 uses the model CENTRAL dispersion 5.10 km/s as if it were the dispersion at the half-light radius 19.76 pc.  Interpolating Baumgardt's measured profile to r_h,l gives 4.77 km/s.  Small on its own -- 0.06 dex -- but it is the same class of substitution as V3 and it also runs toward the claim   (NGC 2419: g05 uses 5.10 km/s (model central); measured profile interpolated to r_h,l = 19.76 pc gives 4.77 km/s, i.e. -0.058 dex)
  [FAIL] V5 (the Pal 14 choice, disclosed by g05 but made the OPPOSITE way to this repository's own convention) g05 takes the LOWER of the two dispersions available for Pal 14 (Jordi et al. 2009, 0.38 km/s) where Baumgardt's bin on the SAME 16 stars gives 0.71.  h93 carries the HIGHER value and says so explicitly: 'The LOWER value makes the framework's over-prediction WORSE, so this script carries the higher one as the framework-favourable choice.'  g05 reverses that convention without saying it did, and it is worth 0.54 dex on the most extreme of the four points   (Pal 14: Jordi 0.38 vs Baumgardt bin 0.71 on the same 16 stars = +0.543 dex; g05's quoted -1.306 becomes -0.763)

