  [PASS] V9 (AND THIS ONE PASSES -- THE DIRECTION OF THE CLAIM SURVIVES EVERYTHING I CAN THROW AT IT) under every dispersion choice, every stellar mass-to-light ratio from 1 to 2, and both a_0 footings, the outer-halo globular clusters still sit BELOW the kernel and the dwarf spheroidals at the same internal acceleration still sit above it.  The qualitative statement -- support type does not predict the sign of the residual -- is not refuted by the input errors.  Only the numbers are   (least negative cluster median over all 24 combinations: -0.264 dex (h93's choice: Baumgardt MEASURED bins at r_h,l, Ups=1.0, canonical); smallest dwarf-minus-cluster gap +0.289 dex)
